# Build context exclusions.
#
# NOTE: artifacts/ is deliberately NOT ignored here. The Dockerfile copies the
# trained model into the image, so excluding it makes `docker build` fail with
# 'failed to calculate checksum ... "/artifacts": not found'. The model stays out
# of *git* via .gitignore; that is a separate concern from the Docker build
# context, and conflating the two breaks the image.

data/
.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
tests/
*.md
.env
.venv/
venv/
# Ignore the training outputs the image does not need. The .joblib must stay.
artifacts/*.png
artifacts/*.csv
artifacts/*.json